  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, talks about the 1947 Roswell incident, a reported crash of a flying object near Roswell, New Mexico. He says a man named Alfred O'Donnell was a source for the journalist Annie Jacobsen's book Area 51, and that, as she said on Lex Fridman's podcast, the craft was a hoax built for Stalin with help from the Nazi doctor Josef Mengele. In another telling Michels names neither O'Donnell nor Stalin, and describes the bodies as aged-looking children used as crash dummies. If true, it would mean Roswell was a human trick, not an alien crash."
